{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996525-time-again","id":996525,"title":"Time again","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-01T04:33:00-07:00","id":996525,"title":"Time again","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=996360#post996360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Normally, when you use Corridors of Time you can only send a target back on its own timeline, and temporal Sympathy doesn't &amp;quot;web&amp;quot; like spatial Sympathy does because Sympathy is maintained between a target and its past selves. Do you think it's possible though to alter your own temporal Sympathy sufficiently to be able to send yourself back in time in someone else's place? Say you have a friend Jim, who's 90, and you're only 30, can you beg, borrow or steal his temporal Sympathy, apply it to youself, and then cast Corridors of Time to go back to when Jim was 20? If you do, who is affected by changes you made in the past? Do you go back and inhabit Jim's 20 year old self, or is his presence temporarily annihilated by yours? Can you think of any other obvious repercussions? What level of Time would this take?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I decided this wasn't really a simple question, so new topic. Expanding on that, s it as simple as Borrow Threads, or is it Patterning? Flat out impossible? What happens if you manage the temporal Pattern swap and do Shifting Sands?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T11:03:22-07:00","id":996695,"title":"","content":"I would posit you inhabit his self if you included a Reach effect to that tune. Otherwise, you simple appear there in that point in space and time as yourself traveling back. Both have their advantages and risks. As for SS, it would work as described, just with the added issue of potentially choosing to inhabit a different body temporarily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T11:16:27-07:00","id":996703,"title":"","content":"Ok, I could see that, and then Jim is rendered non-existent for the Duration since you're replacing him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T11:39:29-07:00","id":996714,"title":"","content":"No, you cannot Borrow Threads Temporal Sympathy, nor can you otherwise manipulate Temporal Sympathy to the point where you have it with someone else's past self. That's just not how Temporal Sympathy works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T11:48:12-07:00","id":996717,"title":"","content":"Ok, why not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T12:46:36-07:00","id":996765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996525-time-again?p=996717#post996717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, why not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Altering past events outside the reach of your personal timeline is the stuff of archmastery and vastly ill-advised use of Shifting Sands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T13:05:12-07:00","id":996773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996525-time-again?p=996717#post996717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, why not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not 12 Arcana instead of 10? Why 5 Paths instead of 360? Why does Knowing come before Veiling? Why is Hung Spell a spell and not an Attainment? Because that's the way the magic system works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T13:50:13-07:00","id":996786,"title":"","content":"I think Mrmdubois is asking for a Doylist explanation. Like 10 Arcana being an improved version of the Ascension system, or Hung Spell as written allowing for targeting foreign spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T14:36:58-07:00","id":996816,"title":"","content":"Surely you must be able to use a Borrow Threads-like effect with Temporal Sympathy, or you wouldn't be able to use it with subjects other than yourself. Or have I totally misunderstood how that attainment works?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T15:01:58-07:00","id":996827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996525-time-again?p=996786#post996786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Mrmdubois is asking for a Doylist explanation. Like 10 Arcana being an improved version of the Ascension system, or Hung Spell as written allowing for targeting foreign spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Temporal Sympathy is a measurement of how much a subject has changed since the time you are affecting it with your spell. It just doesn't make sense to have Temporal Sympathy with something that wasn't your past self, because at no point did that thing change to become your present self. It's not like Sympathetic Connections, which represent relationships between two different subjects. Temporal Sympathy doesn't connect multiple subjects, it's all the same subject, which has changed over time.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Sorry, I guess that was more of a Wattsonian explanation. The Doylist answer would be that Temporal Sympathy exists to allow Time Mages to affect their subjects in the past. Taking someone else's Temporal Sympathy with their past self doesn't really make sense within that framework. What are you even doing at that point? Affecting yourself in the subject's Path? What does that even mean?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996525-time-again?p=996816#post996816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Surely you must be able to use a Borrow Threads-like effect with Temporal Sympathy, or you wouldn't be able to use it with subjects other than yourself. Or have I totally misunderstood how that attainment works?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you might have. What the Attainment allows you to do is use certain Time spells to affect a subject in the past. The more a subject has changed since the time you are affecting it, the weaker the subject's Temporal Sympathy with iteself at that time is, and the more the passage of time Withstands the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-01-2016, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T16:16:28-07:00","id":996869,"title":"","content":"I guess my confusion lies in the fact that you can interfere with a target's past at any point in its past by sending a spell so why can't you send an agent (Inthis particular case yourself)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T16:25:42-07:00","id":996874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996525-time-again?p=996869#post996869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess my confusion lies in the fact that you can interfere with a target's past at any point in its past by sending a spell so why can't you send an agent (Inthis particular case yourself)?</div> </div> </div> </div>You aren't sending a spell back in time, you are targeting a previous version of the subject with the spell. Everything has its own personal timeline, that is the part of their Pattern you affect with Time. That timeline stretches back to when the thing came into existence as a meaningful Pattern, and extends (although not firmly) as far forward as they will exist. Sands of Time and Corridors of Time are Fraying and Unmaking for a reason, you aren't traveling in time, you are destroying that piece of the Time Pattern that is the subjects personal timeline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T16:33:49-07:00","id":996880,"title":"","content":"Ok, that makes sense. Why is a subject'a relation to its temporal sympathy mutable in some ways, making it stronger for instance, and immutable in others for instance copying it to a different pattern? I'll accept it just is, but I'd kind of like more justification than that if it exists (or can be rationalized).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T16:46:20-07:00","id":996885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996525-time-again?p=996880#post996880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, that makes sense. Why is a subject'a relation to its temporal sympathy mutable in some ways, making it stronger for instance, and immutable in others for instance copying it to a different pattern? I'll accept it just is, but I'd kind of like more justification than that if it exists (or can be rationalized).</div> </div> </div> </div>Strengthening or weakening something's Temporal Sympathy is making its pattern more or less like it was at an earlier time. Replacing something's Temporal Sympathy would make it a completely different thing at an earlier time. Theoretically something an Archmaster of Time could do, but not something within the normal capabilities of the Time Arcanum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T17:05:57-07:00","id":996891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996525-time-again?p=996869#post996869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess my confusion lies in the fact that you can interfere with a target's past at any point in its past by sending a spell</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you can't. This has been discussed extensively. The small handful of spells that use Temporal Sympathy mostly use it for calling echoes of information forward or moving the person casting the spell backward in time, which is distinct from casting a spell at a target in the past because spells don't exist before they're cast and therefore have no sympathy to move along without also shifting their point of origin, hence the stipulation on combined-casting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T20:03:00-07:00","id":996961,"title":"","content":"If you cast a spell on a target that exists, it takes effect in the present unless you happen to already be in the past. <br /> <br /> As the system presents it, to cast on a person in the past would require casting Corridors on yourself to get back to the desired time and casting it. (Pre-revision, though, I think the attainment <i>did</i> allow that.) This would limit you to traveling back within your lifespan. <br /> <br /> None of that logically precludes a spell that allows thread hijacking, just that it would be at least Weaving and probably Patterning. You are doing something with it that isn't in its normal range of possibility.<br /> <br /> Making really <i>should</i> be able to extend one's time-line back, too, come to think on it.<br /> <br /> That said, if you wanted to make a spell appear in the past, a Making effect to give it a time to weave into history would make some sense, as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}